# Delicious.com

> Delicious.com tells you what to eat today, writes the recipes, adapts them to the
> ingredients you already have, and builds your grocery list. A fresh full-day menu —
> breakfast, lunch, dinner and dessert — is published every morning, each dish with
> real, verified macros (calories, protein, carbs, fat).

Delicious.com is a daily meal-planning site and recipe archive. Unlike a static recipe
blog, its core is a **new complete menu every day** plus tools to plan a week, generate
a custom plan, cook from your pantry or leftovers, and turn any plan into one combined,
aisle-sorted grocery list you can export or send to Instacart, Walmart and Kroger.

## What makes it distinctive
- A fresh breakfast/lunch/dinner/dessert menu is generated **every morning** — the site answers "what should I cook today?" before you ask.
- **Pantry remix / fridge scanner:** photograph your fridge or list what you have, and it builds a real recipe around it, listing only the few extras to buy.
- **Every recipe carries full macros** (calories, protein, carbs, fat), verified against a nutrition database where possible.
- **One grocery list** from any plan — deduplicated, aisle-sorted, pantry-aware, exportable to PDF/Excel/CSV.
- ~3,600 real recipes with ingredients, method and macros.

